<title>GERMANY: AgrEvo won't rule out listing.</title>
<headline>AgrEvo won't rule out listing.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>German crop protection products group AgrEvo, a unit of Hoechst AG and Schering AG, made no specific announcement on Friday about plans to go public, but said floating its shares was still an option.</p>
<p>AgrEvo chief executive Gerhard Prante told reporters &quot;a bourse listing is an option&quot; but stressed that no final decision had been reached.</p>
<p>Speculation has been growing that AgrEvo, which earlier said it would post a one-third improvement in 1996 operating profits, would soon be ready to be floated on the bourse.</p>
</text>
